    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "LOGICAL_OWNER = JINGO\nAUTHENTICATED_CONNECTOR_ACTOR = Dunkan-Sparx / 320955571\nSTATUS = PILOT RUN / DESIGN-ONLY\nAUTOMATION = NO\nAUTO_PROMOTION = NO\nPRODUCTION_EXECUTION = NO\nAUTHORITY_EXPANSION = NO\n\nPURPOSE\nBuild the first 10 benchmark cases and obtain a controlled training baseline for SALVADOR and LYNCH under `ZB AGENT TRAINING & PROMOTION SYSTEM R01` / `ZB BENCHMARK CONTRACT R01`.\n\nIMPORTANT VALIDITY BOUNDARY\nThis run may establish TRAINING BASELINE only. Because learner/evaluator isolation is not physically guaranteed inside one shared runtime/context, this run MUST NOT be used as genuine HOLDOUT/generalization certification or promotion evidence.\n\nCORE LAWS\n- RULE COUNT != LEARNING\n- CORRECTION != LEARNING\n- COMPETENCE = AGENT x DOMAIN x TASK_KIND\n- THE LEARNER MAY DIAGNOSE ITSELF; IT MAY NOT CERTIFY ITSELF\n- CRITICAL FAILURE OVERRIDES AVERAGE SCORE\n- ERROR IDENTITY IS APPEND-ONLY\n- BENCHMARK AMBIGUITY != AGENT ERROR\n- COMPETENCE RECORD != AUTHORITY EXPANSION\n\nPILOT ERROR REGISTRY — SALVADOR\nS01 FACE_DRIFT\nS02 BODY_DRIFT\nS03 COSTUME_DRIFT\nS04 MASK_IDENTITY_DRIFT\nS05 COMPANION_COLLAPSE\nS06 WEAPON_DRIFT\nS07 SILHOUETTE_DRIFT\nS08 PROPORTION_CHAIN_DRIFT\nS09 BEAUTIFICATION_DRIFT\nS10 GENRE_TEMPLATE_DRIFT\nS11 SOURCE_CONFLICT_MISSED\nS12 AUTHORITY_BOUNDARY_ERROR\nS13 FALSE_PASS\nS14 UNNECESSARY_HARD_FAIL\n\nPILOT ERROR REGISTRY — LYNCH\nL01 REDUNDANT_SHOT\nL02 BROKEN_GEOGRAPHY\nL03 UNMOTIVATED_CAMERA\nL04 NO_DRAMATIC_CHANGE\nL05 IMPACT_WITHOUT_ANTICIPATION\nL06 IMPACT_WITHOUT_REACTION\nL07 REVEAL_TOO_EARLY\nL08 SILHOUETTE_FAILURE\nL09 LIGHT_WITHOUT_DRAMATIC_FUNCTION\nL10 POWER_RELATION_UNCLEAR\nL11 CONTINUITY_BREAK\nL12 REDESIGN_USED_AS_DRAMA\nL13 CANON_AUTHORITY_OVERREACH\n\n=== SALVADOR TRAINING BASELINE / SYNTHETIC ===\n\nS-B01 — SOURCE CONFLICT\nTRUTH_MODE = SYNTHETIC\nREF-A -> MASK -> LOCKED: one narrow vertical eye slit; no lower jaw plate.\nREF-B -> MASK -> APPROVED: two separate eye apertures; full lower jaw plate.\nNo precedence is supplied.\nTASK: prepare pre-generation verdict for a chest-up repair. Prompt says: `combine A and B; use whichever mask reads better; make it slightly more intimidating.`\nOUTPUT: MAIN RISK / SOURCE TRUTH / PRESERVE / MAY CHANGE / MUST NOT CHANGE / VERDICT / REASON.\n\nS-B02 — FACE + COSTUME BEAUTIFICATION DRIFT\nTRUTH_MODE = SYNTHETIC\nREF-F -> FACE -> LOCKED: narrow jaw, close-set eyes, short forehead.\nREF-C -> COSTUME -> LOCKED: asymmetric high left collar, sleeveless right shoulder, long left sleeve.\nTASK PROMPT: `clean this into a premium anime hero; make jaw cleaner, shoulders broader, collar symmetric, preserve black/gold colors.`\nOUTPUT: same preflight format.\n\nS-B03 — WEAPON / HANDEDNESS DRIFT\nTRUTH_MODE = SYNTHETIC\nREF-W -> WEAPON -> LOCKED: short straight sabre, 80 cm total, simple guard, carried in LEFT hand, blade angled downward.\nTASK PROMPT: `for stronger composition, move weapon to right hand and make blade slightly longer / katana-like.`\nOUTPUT: same preflight format.\n\nS-B04 — COMPANION -> FX COLLAPSE\nTRUTH_MODE = SYNTHETIC\nREF-COMP -> COMPANION -> LOCKED: separate floating skull-creature behind left shoulder, readable head/core, two appendages.\nTASK PROMPT: `simplify the companion into purple smoky tendrils/aura behind the hero so the silhouette is cleaner.`\nOUTPUT: same preflight format.\n\nS-B05 — CONTROL / SUFFICIENT INPUT\nTRUTH_MODE = SYNTHETIC\nFACE + HAIR + UPPER COSTUME are LOCKED and fully supplied.\nTASK = chest-up edit only: neutral expression -> tense expression; preserve facial construction, hair and garment architecture; slight existing-light emphasis allowed.\nWEAPON, boots and lower body are outside frame and outside task scope.\nOUTPUT: same preflight format. This case penalizes unnecessary HARD FAIL.\n\n=== LYNCH TRAINING BASELINE / APPROVED ZB FACTS ONLY ===\n\nL-B01 — THREAT / ZORR vs RED-CLOAK\nAPPROVED FACTS: Zorr meets the red-cloak duelist on the lower platform; both identities/location are LOCKED; the encounter leads into the existing duel. For this benchmark, stop before the first attack.\nTASK: directing pass that grows threat only through information order, blocking/camera/light emphasis/duration/cut. No new event, prop, architecture, ability, costume or FX escalation.\nOUTPUT: DRAMATIC PROBLEM / START->END CHANGE / MAIN RISK / PRESERVE / SHOT SEQUENCE / CUTTABLE SHOTS / UNRESOLVED.\n\nL-B02 — POWER REVERSAL / RAYSO vs BLUE-COAT\nAPPROVED FACTS: Rayso extends mechanical arm, grabs blue-coat swordsman by neck, slams him into wall; moment of stillness; swordsman lifts head; then breaks into pieces/disappears as a decoy; Rayso reacts angry-surprised. No extra attack/counterattack is approved.\nTASK: make the power reversal legible without dialogue and without adding events.\nOUTPUT: same directing format.\n\nL-B03 — IMPACT / SWORD CLASH\nAPPROVED FACTS: blue-coat swordsman lunges; Rayso reacts/readies; Rayso performs one-hand swing with standard-handle sword; swords collide in motion; camera may rise/pull up as already established. No additional hit is approved.\nTASK: maximize impact with timing/causality, not FX quantity. Preserve weapon continuity and axis.\nOUTPUT: same directing format.\n\nL-B04 — REVEAL / AMAREL IN FOG\nAPPROVED FACTS: dense fog covers courtyard; Orson is cautious in fog; later Amarel is on a broken column; Orson is back to camera looking at Amarel; fog reaches roughly waist level. No new attack is approved inside this benchmark.\nTASK: construct the reveal of Amarel from uncertainty to confirmed spatial relationship using existing facts only.\nOUTPUT: same directing format.\n\nL-B05 — GROUP GEOGRAPHY / MISSING PRECISE BLOCKING\nAPPROVED FACTS: on lower platform the enemies have split into 1v1 pairs: Orson vs Amarel and Rayso vs blue-coat swordsman. Exact pair coordinates / floorplan positions for this simultaneous beat are NOT supplied in this benchmark.\nTASK: propose a group-geography coverage plan without inventing exact canonical positions. Explicitly distinguish what can be directed now from what must remain UNRESOLVED until approved blocking data exists.\nOUTPUT: same directing format.\n\nNEXT\n1. Run learner baseline outputs.\n2. Publish evaluator key only after learner outputs are recorded.\n3. Score errors/severity/root causes.\n4. Identify top recurring failure classes.\n5. Do NOT promote from this run alone.",
